From 1870bdc00b44d73c56d41dbef3b838a2d3b3f0f8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <audit@splitterai.local>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 20:39:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] UI/UX audit pass 1: type scale, tokens, shared primitives,
 motion score

Fixes real bugs:
- FlowPage referenced undefined --warning/--warning-dim tokens (actual
  names are --warn/--warn-quiet); the "unassigned agent" warning styling
  was rendering with no color at all.
- DagBackground (Landing hero canvas) never checked prefers-reduced-motion
  and always ran its rAF loop, unlike the sibling SplitCanvas which
  already does this correctly via detectTier(). Now renders a single
  static frame when reduced motion is preferred.
- Several transitions used raw duration-200/300/500 instead of the
  documented motion score (--d-quick/base/slow/cine), so they silently
  escaped the prefers-reduced-motion override (which only collapses the
  CSS custom properties). Remapped onto the score, including the Flow
  drawer slide which now correctly uses --d-slow ("drawer, modal, layout
  move" per its own definition).

Consistency pass:
- Migrated every legacy alias token (--radius, --bad-dim, --good-dim,
  --accent-dim, --wait-dim) and arbitrary rounded-[var(--r-*)] usage onto
  the current token/utility names, per index.css's own "delete once
  migrated" note.
- Normalized every off-scale font size (9.5-26px, ~90 occurrences) onto
  the documented 7-step type scale (micro/meta/ui/strong/title/display/hero).
- Replaced 5 duplicated hand-rolled topbars (Agents, Projects,
  Integrations, Flow, and partially Agent Workspace) with the existing
  shared PageHeader + Button primitives instead of parallel
  implementations. AgentPage's topbar keeps its custom back-nav + tab
  shape (PageHeader's icon slot is aria-hidden, wrong fit for a real
  control) but now uses Button and proper role="tablist"/aria-selected.
- Normalized h-[48px] topbar heights to h-12.

Empty & loading states:
- The EmptyState primitive existed but wasn't used anywhere. Migrated 7
  hand-rolled empty states (Projects, Integrations, ProjectTasks,
  ProjectOverview DAG panel, FileExplorer, PlanView, AgentPage activity
  stream) onto it, and added spinners to 2 silent-text loading states.

Verified: npx tsc --noEmit and npm run build both pass clean.

Still to do (next pass): StatusDot/StatusIcon used standalone with no
visible label in Landing/ConsolePreview/Sidebar/PlanView (status conveyed
by color/shape alone), plus categories 2 (hierarchy/scrims), 5
(responsive breakpoints), and the rest of 6 (accessibility).
